# core/data/talk/grammar/en/surf_e_topic.tlk - topic-slot lines, push E (owner: TK; T5B-SURF5).
# Every line names the topic ({x}, {x:cap}). Clean in any room: no register word, no romance,
# no cool or tease act, nothing aimed at the player. Grief topics go to the grief bank.
# Rule names start with se_. Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.

@rule core.opine_pos.se_pos_a guard: topic act: agree
  "{x:cap} is a good one, and I'm not just being polite about it."
  "I'd happily have {x} on the table every day of the week."
  "Oh, I like {x}. It's the sort of thing that makes a day better."
  "{x:cap} gets my vote. Not that there's a ballot, but still."
@rule core.opine_pos.se_pos_b guard: topic act: agree
  "I'm a sucker for {x}. Always have been, always will be."
  "{x:cap} is quietly one of the best things around here."
  "Yes, {x}. I think about it more than I'd ever admit out loud."
  "Nice choice, {x}. You've got a knack for picking the good ones."
@rule core.opine_neg.se_neg_a guard: topic act: disagree
  "{x:cap} and I don't really get along. We've agreed to be polite."
  "Honestly, {x} just isn't my scene. Sorry, I know it's a letdown."
  "I'd rather not spend much time on {x}, if that's alright with you."
  "{x:cap}? I'll be polite, but I'm not keen on it."
@rule core.opine_neg.se_neg_b guard: topic act: disagree
  "No, {x} doesn't do it for me. I'm sure it's lovely for others."
  "I find {x} a bit dull, if I'm honest. Nothing personal."
  "{x:cap} has had its day, as far as I'm concerned."
@rule core.answer.se_ans_a guard: topic act: backchannel
  "{x:cap}? I'd say it's a bit of a mixed bag. Good and bad."
  "On {x}, I'll give you my honest take. It's not the whole story."
  "Ah, {x}. The short answer is yes, the long one is more fun."
  "{x:cap}, you say? I've got a few opinions. Want them all?"
@rule core.answer.se_ans_b guard: topic act: backchannel
  "{x:cap} is something I'd rather show you than explain."
  "I'd answer {x} with a question of my own. Are you asking for fun?"
  "{x:cap}? It depends whether we're being serious or silly."
  "Good thinking, {x}. I'd need to sleep on that before I answer."
@rule core.joke.se_joke_a guard: topic act: laugh
  "{x:cap}? Ha! That's the best thing I've heard all morning."
  "Oh, {x}. You've set me off now, I can't stop giggling."
  "Hah, {x}! I'd say that's a proper joke, and a good one."
  "{x:cap} with a punchline like that? Well played, I say."
@rule core.joke.se_joke_b guard: topic act: laugh
  "Ha, {x}! Don't tell me that's your whole act. I'm impressed."
  "{x:cap} is funny, but you're funnier for saying it."
  "Hee, {x}. I'll be thinking about that all afternoon."
@rule core.tell.se_tell_a guard: topic act: backchannel
  "Oh, {x}! Where do I even start? It's a long story, but a good one."
  "{x:cap} is a subject I could talk about for ages, so brace yourself."
  "Right, {x}. Picture it: a normal day, and then this happened."
  "I've got a whole pile of thoughts on {x}. Here's the best bit."
@rule core.tell.se_tell_b guard: topic act: backchannel
  "{x:cap} came up once before, and it turned out differently than I thought."
  "The trick with {x} is to ignore what everyone else says about it."
  "{x:cap}, eh. I'll tell you a thing I've never told anyone."
@rule core.agree.se_agree_a guard: topic act: agree
  "Yes, {x}. You've put that better than I ever could."
  "{x:cap}, exactly. I was just about to say the same thing."
  "You're right about {x}. Let's agree on that and be done."
@rule core.disagree.se_disagree_a guard: topic act: disagree
  "I see {x} differently, but I'll hear you out on it."
  "Hmm, not about {x}. I'd put it another way, but it's close."
  "{x:cap}? I'd push back on that, just a little."
@rule core.change_topic.se_chg_a guard: topic act: answer
  "{x:cap}, why not? Anything beats the last subject, honestly."
  "Let's move on to {x}. My head's been stuck on the last thing."
  "{x:cap}, good call. We needed a change of scene."
